%description:

TcpCubic.cntClamp:linux -- before the first loss, the window grows by one segment for each 20 ACKs or faster.

The claim (TcpCubic.ned): "cap on the per-increment ACK count while no W_max is known: before
the first loss, and after each RTO, which clears W_max".

The classes: linux (20, the default, the value of Linux) and tight (a smaller value), invalid
(below 0). The code: while no W_max is known, the ACK count of one increment is at most the
value (TcpCubic::update()). This test separates "linux" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, with TcpCubic, an initial threshold of 8000 bytes and without the
Reno-friendly estimate (preconditions: the estimate grows faster than the clamp), which sends
without a loss to host2, whose window is 1000000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms.
Observation: level 3, at 1.5 s, the window is below 100000 bytes (about 39000): about one segment for each 20 ACKs.

%# parameter: TcpCubic.cntClamp
%# class: linux
%# value: 20
%# key: *.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.cntClamp
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpCubicCntClampLinux")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(1.5)
                 .describe("the window at 1.5 s")
                 .assertModule("host1.tcp.conn-*", "state.snd_cwnd < 100000"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpCubicCntClampLinux compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.cntClamp = 20    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpCubic"
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.tcp.initialSsthresh = 8000
*.host1.tcp.conn-*.algorithm.tcpFriendliness = false
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1000000
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000000B
sim-time-limit = 2s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpCubicCntClampLinux: PASS
